WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.560
A receptor writes phosphotyrosine marks across its tail.

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:08.280
How can one protein find the right mark among all the others?

3
00:00:11.833 --> 00:00:16.913
Phosphate changes a small surface patch, but the mark usually does little alone.

4
00:00:18.233 --> 00:00:20.693
It becomes useful when a reader binds there.

5
00:00:21.913 --> 00:00:25.993
The reader brings its host protein into the growing signaling complex.

6
00:00:27.373 --> 00:00:30.593
A kinase writes the mark, and a phosphatase can erase it.

7
00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:34.227
An SH2 domain is one such reader.

8
00:00:35.547 --> 00:00:38.087
Its first binding pocket fits phosphotyrosine.

9
00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:42.447
Positively charged side chains help grip the phosphate.

10
00:00:43.887 --> 00:00:48.367
Unmodified tyrosine lacks that phosphate, so the pocket cannot make the same

11
00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:49.367
contact.

12
00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:53.927
That first pocket answers whether tyrosine is phosphorylated.

13
00:00:55.147 --> 00:00:58.367
It cannot identify which phosphorylated site this is.

14
00:00:59.387 --> 00:01:04.667
A neighbouring surface reads residues beside the phosphotyrosine and supplies

15
00:01:04.667 --> 00:01:06.167
another layer of preference.

16
00:01:07.587 --> 00:01:11.287
Different SH2 domains carry differently shaped neighbouring surfaces.

17
00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:14.910
Now the reader tests both features together.

18
00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:18.550
Several tails offer the same gold phosphate.

19
00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.470
Their neighbouring patterns differ.

20
00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:26.730
Matching blocks settle into the groove; poor fits make the reader release.

21
00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:32.130
Src-family readers favour one pattern, while other readers favour others.

22
00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:40.600
Here is the rule. Reusable binding domains turn recognized motifs or lipids into

23
00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:41.600
protein connections.

24
00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:48.920
For SH2, phosphorylation enables the contact, while sequence context helps choose

25
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:50.180
among possible partners.

26
00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:54.460
The domain binds; it does not catalyse a reaction.

27
00:01:55.583 --> 00:01:57.523
Predict before the reader moves.

28
00:01:58.883 --> 00:02:00.723
Both tails carry phosphotyrosine.

29
00:02:02.023 --> 00:02:05.023
Only the lower neighbouring pattern fits this reader's groove.

30
00:02:06.363 --> 00:02:08.103
Which tail will retain the reader longer?

31
00:02:09.503 --> 00:02:11.483
Watch both parts of the binding surface.

32
00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:22.750
The lower tail makes both contacts, so it retains this reader more strongly in this

33
00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:26.150
comparison. The upper tail still has phosphate.

34
00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:31.490
Its neighbouring pattern simply provides a poorer fit for this domain.

35
00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:36.230
Another SH2 domain could prefer a different pattern.

36
00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:41.900
The domain is modular because it keeps this binding activity when moved.

37
00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:44.940
Detach the reader from one host.

38
00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:50.220
Attach it to a different host, and its preferred target remains the same.

39
00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:55.020
The new host can bring a different cellular activity to that site.

40
00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:57.850
Preference is not destiny.

41
00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:04.750
Location, abundance, timing, and the rest of the host protein also shape contacts in

42
00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:10.790
cells. The domain narrows the candidates; cellular context narrows them further.

43
00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:15.850
A preferred motif cannot recruit a reader that never reaches it.

44
00:03:16.833 --> 00:03:20.233
Other modules apply the same logic to other targets.

45
00:03:21.593 --> 00:03:27.053
SH3 reads proline-rich motifs, while some PH domains read membrane lipids.

46
00:03:28.173 --> 00:03:31.793
The target changes, but recognition still creates a connection.

47
00:03:33.133 --> 00:03:35.533
For PH, that connection is to the membrane.
